(6143395, 904473, 99263, '<td valign="top">That ain''t a ladybug imo. Whilst there are thousands of different species the long feelers give this one away. Ladybugs have short, stubby antennae with a roundish little disc at the end of them. That''s an Asian bug of some kind. Here''s some very good info and a field guide on ladybugs.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.nhm.org/site/activities-programs/community-science/lost-ladybug-project/identifying-ladybugs" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.nhm.org/site/activities-programs/community-science/lost-ladybug-project/identifying-ladybugs</a> <br/><a href="//www.discoverlife.org/mp/20q?guide=Ladybug&amp;cl=llp" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.discoverlife.org/mp/20q?guide=Ladybug&amp;cl=llp</a> <br/><a href="//everything-ladybug.com/anatomy/morphology.htm" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//everything-ladybug.com/anatomy/morphology.htm</a> <br/><a href="//www.ladybug-life-cycle.com/ladybug-anatomy.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.ladybug-life-cycle.com/ladybug-anatomy.html</a> <br/><a href="//everything-ladybug.com/ladybug-anatomy.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//everything-ladybug.com/ladybug-anatomy.html</a> <br/> <br/>But a nicely captured close-up none the less :)</td>', 'That ain''t a ladybug imo. Whilst there are thousands of different species the long feelers give this one away. Ladybugs have short, stubby antennae with a roundish little disc at the end of them. That''s an Asian bug of some kind. Here''s some very good info and a field guide on ladybugs. //www.nhm.org/site/activities-programs/community-science/lost-ladybug-project/identifying-ladybugs //www.discoverlife.org/mp/20q?guide=Ladybug&cl=llp //everything-ladybug.com/anatomy/morphology.htm //www.ladybug-life-cycle.com/ladybug-anatomy.html //everything-ladybug.com/ladybug-anatomy.html  But a nicely captured close-up none the less :)', '2010-08-28 04:22:14.000000', NULL, 1),
