(6149547, 904979, 59029, '<td valign="top">Hi Katie!<br/> <br/>OK, here''s your unofficial critique on your daisy shot. *cracking knuckles* :-)<br/> <br/>Tecnhically, in terms of composition, there is nothing wrong with it.  Rule of thirds, nice dof to let the flowers face-on to the camera pop especially as most of the others have lost their petals already.  That unforgiving 9 am light hasn''t killed the colours too much and I like the backlit effect you did manage to get.<br/> <br/>Artistically, though, as another commenter noted, it''s very tough to stand out in a challenge like this with so many flower shots!  Daisies, black-eyed susans, sunflowers and the like are just too easy to find and shoot.  It''s a pleasant enough shot but just doesn''t have the crucial WOW factor that tends to be favoured here (or the heavy-handed saturation).  It''s just too easy to anticipate a shot like this, in a challenge like this.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps, I know you''re a killer photog at what you like to shoot!  FWIW if one were handy, I might have tried to shoehorn in a palomino ;-)<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Hi Katie! OK, here''s your unofficial critique on your daisy shot. *cracking knuckles* :-) Tecnhically, in terms of composition, there is nothing wrong with it.  Rule of thirds, nice dof to let the flowers face-on to the camera pop especially as most of the others have lost their petals already.  That unforgiving 9 am light hasn''t killed the colours too much and I like the backlit effect you did manage to get. Artistically, though, as another commenter noted, it''s very tough to stand out in a challenge like this with so many flower shots!  Daisies, black-eyed susans, sunflowers and the like are just too easy to find and shoot.  It''s a pleasant enough shot but just doesn''t have the crucial WOW factor that tends to be favoured here (or the heavy-handed saturation).  It''s just too easy to anticipate a shot like this, in a challenge like this. Hope this helps, I know you''re a killer photog at what you like to shoot!  FWIW if one were handy, I might have tried to shoehorn in a palomino ;-) Susan', '2010-09-02 09:10:02.000000', NULL, 0),
