(6152457, 905219, 52336, '<td valign="top">If you consider this photo in relation to the differences between it and the one next to it, the impact is reduced, since they''re virtually identical.  Some discussion on what you did to set up light, how you posed the model, and what all this means to you would help in appreciating it more.</td>', 'If you consider this photo in relation to the differences between it and the one next to it, the impact is reduced, since they''re virtually identical.  Some discussion on what you did to set up light, how you posed the model, and what all this means to you would help in appreciating it more.', '2010-09-05 12:02:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6152498, 905219, 93421, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Louis:</b></div><hr/><i> If you consider this photo in relation to the differences between it and the one next to it, the impact is reduced, since they''re virtually identical.  Some discussion on what you did to set up light, how you posed the model, and what all this means to you would help in appreciating it more. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Louis.  This was shot using a single silver reflector and available natural light.  The model held the piece of yellow fabric above her head and the light was reflected through the fabric onto the right side of her face.  This was my first attempt at a model shoot using only available natural light (and a reflector) - trying to learn something new.  I''m also not a fan of shooting people so also trying to push myself in that area to.</td>', 'Originally posted by Louis: If you consider this photo in relation to the differences between it and the one next to it, the impact is reduced, since they''re virtually identical.  Some discussion on what you did to set up light, how you posed the model, and what all this means to you would help in appreciating it more.   Hi Louis.  This was shot using a single silver reflector and available natural light.  The model held the piece of yellow fabric above her head and the light was reflected through the fabric onto the right side of her face.  This was my first attempt at a model shoot using only available natural light (and a reflector) - trying to learn something new.  I''m also not a fan of shooting people so also trying to push myself in that area to.', '2010-09-05 12:54:41.000000', NULL, 0),
